solves: |
  Companies spend enormous energy trying to manufacture innovation—hack days, offsites, suggestion boxes—while ignoring the quieter, more damaging failure:
  <strong>ideas dying in the space between insight and response.</strong>

  Employees notice inefficiencies and better ways of working every day. But raising those ideas often means waiting for a 1:1, navigating politics, or convincing a manager who may not have the context, incentives, or safety to advance them.
  Over time, people learn that speaking up isn’t worth the effort—and leadership never hears the ideas it is actively asking for.

  <strong>Insight A[i]gent exists to close that gap in real time</strong>—with memory, context, routing, and closure.

