note: |
  <strong>Innovation doesn’t fail because employees lack ideas.</strong> It fails because organizations introduce friction, fear, and delay between insight and response.

  This tool is not about replacing managers. It removes early-stage failure modes—without removing accountability—so ideas aren’t lost before they ever have a chance to be evaluated.
  <strong>Humans retain final authority.</strong>

